// ============================================================================
//  ID:             Q05  (report appendix: A4, "Web shell commands")
//  Name:           Web shell commands
//  Purpose:        Pull every request to the web shell so its commands can be decoded.
//  Hunt step:      5, 7, 8, 10, 12 and 13
//  ATT&CK:         T1505.003 Server Software Component: Web Shell
//                  T1059.004 Command and Scripting Interpreter: Unix Shell
//                  T1027 Obfuscated Files or Information
//                  T1016 System Network Configuration Discovery
//                  T1552.001 Unsecured Credentials: Credentials In Files
//                  T1053.003 Scheduled Task/Job: Cron
//                  T1036.005 Masquerading: Match Legitimate Name or Location
//                  T1041 Exfiltration Over C2 Channel
//  Tables:         HartwellHTTPEnriched_CL
//  Time range:     2026-10-23 04:00 to 16:00 UTC
//  Environment:    Practice lab
//  Hit looks like: Requests to /health-check.php carrying a custom header with an encoded command.
//  Result:         Commands were wrapped in Base64 and ROT13. Decoded, they show network discovery,
//                  reading wp-config.php, dumping wp_users, cron persistence, and Base64 exfiltration.
//  Decoding:       Decode each header value with Base64 first, then ROT13. The decoding step was
//                  done outside the saved queries and is not included here.
//  Benign noise:   None expected. Any request to this path is suspicious.
//  Tuning notes:   Change the URI for another web shell name.
//  Changed from the report: removed a trailing comma after request_headers in the project line,
//                  which is a syntax error.
//  Author / date:  Cai Spice · hunt run 2026-10-23, documented 2026-11-20
// ============================================================================

HartwellHTTPEnriched_CL
| where OriginalTime between (datetime(2026-10-23T04:00:00Z) .. datetime(2026-10-23T16:00:00Z))
| where uri == "/health-check.php"
| project OriginalTime, id_orig_h, request_headers
| order by OriginalTime asc
